## 2. Client Portal (login-gated)

### 2.1 Dashboard
- Active & past quote requests
- Job status tracker (per job/PO)
- Downloadable invoices/POs history

### 2.2 Profile
- Company details, saved contact info for faster repeat quote requests

---

## 3. Admin Dashboard (Bee Cee staff only)

### 3.1 Leads / Quote Requests
- Incoming quote requests from site, status management (New → Quoted → Won/Lost)

### 3.2 Fleet & Availability Calendar
- Mark vehicles booked/available by date — prevents double-booking, powers the public "Available" indicator

### 3.3 Job / PO Tracker
- Log PO number, client, service, amount, status (Pending → Delivered → Paid)
- Mirrors their current paper-based PO workflow (CHAZ, Oxfam, PATH, National Assembly POs) but centralized

### 3.4 Client Records
- Client contact list, quote/job history per client

### 3.5 Notifications
- Email/SMS trigger when a quote is sent or job status changes (client sees update in portal)

---

## 4. Suggested Build Phases

| Phase | Includes | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Phase 1 — Launch** | Sections 1.1–1.9 (full public site), basic Quote Request form → email | Gets them a credible, lead-generating site fast |
| **Phase 2 — Dashboard** | Admin Dashboard (3.1–3.3) + Fleet Availability | Internal ops value, matches church-website scope |
| **Phase 3 — Client Portal** | Client login, job tracking, notifications (2.1–2.2, 3.4–3.5) | Adds the "futurized" self-service layer |

This phasing lets them start using and paying for value early, while Phase 2–3 become natural upsells once they see Phase 1 working.

